WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.542
Structured data follows a stable arrangement.

00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:08.912
Relational databases are a classic example because each row follows a known set of columns and types.

00:00:08.912 --> 00:00:13.047
CSV and Parquet files can also contain structured data.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:18.382
The benefit is predictability. We can validate and query fields consistently.

00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:21.032
But structured does not mean correct.

00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:26.632
A structured table can still contain duplicates, missing values, inconsistent categories,

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:28.492
or impossible measurements.

00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:34.667
A useful project question is: what preparation step is required before analysis can even begin?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:39.622
A relational table may be ready for profiling, JSON may need flattening, and free text may need NLP or another

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:42.912
extraction step.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:47.992
The form of the data changes the engineering path, but it does not by itself tell us whether the data is

00:00:47.992 --> 00:00:49.520
high quality.
